  "notes": "Gospel-rooted diva pop, windowed to the 1990s exactly as the research does — the 1980s catalogue is out of scope, which also clears Gate 2. The ballads run 51–75 with a half-time feel and the backbeat on 3, so `halfTime` is true and the snare is `halftime_3`; the 104–130 dance/R&B band is the straight-time wing and is named here rather than encoded. The 1998–99 R&B singles are described as \"a swung 16th programmed kit with stacked claps and a shuffled ghost snare\", which is the warrant for the 0.56 swing and for a ghost probability of 0.34 — the highest on the ballad bench — with the clap offset widened. The third delta is the ballad opening itself: \"ballads open with no drums at all, then a slow kick 1/3 and a heavy snare on 3 with a 16th hat\". Harmony is gospel-voiced I–IV and vi–ii–V with plagal IV–I cadences, all three authored as families, and the extensions lean to sevenths. The melody rule is precise and is encoded literally: \"gospel melisma on the *ends* of phrases while the phrase itself is stepwise\", so the lead is stepwise with `endVariation` on and the ad-lib layer lives in the counter. ⚠ `confidence` is medium because the research rates it high-medium. ⚠ The **INFERRED** parameters are the drum probabilities, `swing.amount` 0.56 and `bpm.mode` 63.",
